@* Markdown cheat sheet shown under the editors.
   <details>/<summary> is a built-in HTML fold-out: clicking the summary
   shows or hides the content, no JavaScript needed. *@
<details class="md-help">
    <summary>Formatting help</summary>
    <table>
        <tr><td><code>**bold**</code></td><td><strong>bold</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>*italic*</code></td><td><em>italic</em></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>## Heading</code></td><td>Heading</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>- item</code></td><td>Bullet list</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>1. item</code></td><td>Numbered list</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>&gt; quote</code></td><td>Quote</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[text](https://…)</code></td><td>Link</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>![description](/media/12)</code></td><td>Image (use <strong>Insert</strong> in the image library)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>`code`</code></td><td><code>code</code></td></tr>
    </table>
    <p class="form-hint">A blank line starts a new paragraph.</p>
</details>
